				"to": "00:00:50,880"
			},
			"offsets": {
				"from": 47040,
				"to": 50880
			},
			"text": " Right. So you've got some dedicated hardware in there to prevent SCR latch-up."
		},
		{
			"timestamps": {
				"from": "00:00:50,880",
				"to": "00:00:59,320"
			},
			"offsets": {
				"from": 50880,
				"to": 59320
			},
			"text": " Yeah, so those are really kind of useful for detecting high transients beyond QR."
		},
		{
			"timestamps": {
				"from": "00:00:59,320",
				"to": "00:01:09,900"
			},
			"offsets": {
				"from": 59320,
				"to": 69900
			},
			"text": " Yeah, so you don't get transient spikes, because that's what SCR latch-up will do is basically shorts out your rail, if you don't know, shorts out your voltage rail, so you'll get this large spike that is not part of normal things."
		},
		{
